y","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The deploy defaults in infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:97-99 and the alarm ModelId dimensions in infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf:80-135 change in the same commit'","T12: 'a one-shot behavior change to all traffic with no flag and no rollback path = MAJOR'","Plan notes an explicitly pinned 4.x model keeps working via PRIOR_GENERATION_WINDOWS — i.e. revert is likely cheap, but this is not stated as the rollback path"],"finding":"The plan flips the production deploy defaults (`docker-compose.yml:97-99`) and the terraform alarm `ModelId` dimensions (`monitoring_eb6e.tf:80-135`) to the 5.5 ids in a single commit, routing all production model traffic to the new models at once, but states no rollback path and no staged rollout / canary. It names a sibling post-deploy metrics-check task and before/after parity runs, yet never says how to quickly undo a bad cutover.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3044d4e02f2823e7","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'The deploy defaults ... and the alarm ModelId dimensions ... change in the same commit'; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n7ee35598dd56db65","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["5.5 Opus/Sonnet/Haiku behave worse than expected in production after the cutover and an operator needs to revert quickly","The post-deploy metrics check (itchy-neutral-whooper) finds Bedrock is not publishing under the new ids and the alarms go blind"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a Rollback note: reverting the single cutover commit restores the 4.x deploy defaults and alarm dimensions with no data cleanup, and any explicitly-pinned 4.x model continues to work; state whether production is cut over all at once or staged.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirm